# Tests

Test names are the spec: reading `test/` should list every rule the SDK enforces.

## With the change

Land behavior and the test that proves it in the same diff. A behavior change without a test is unfinished unless the change is trivial (typo, comment, version bump only).

## Names

- Full sentence, lowercase, no “should”.
- One invariant per `it()` (this repo uses `describe` groups in places; new tests can use top-level `it()` when the file is already flat).

## What to test

- HTTP shape: URL path, method, JSON body, multipart fields — use the existing `mockClient` helpers in `test/helpers.ts`.
- Slug and rename behavior belongs in `test/schema-slug.test.ts` or endpoint tests in `test/parse.test.ts`, not duplicated across files.

## Before claiming API compatibility

If the task is “match doc2json reboot”, grep doc2json for the operation and add a test that would have failed on the old SDK behavior.
